          }
        },
        "80d3ee7d-e860-4a9c-8b84-2c5508cdf136": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": true,
            "title": "Operating & Maintaining",
            "text": "<p>1) Press the selection dial in the centre of the control panel to access the main menu. Rotate the dial to scroll across the menu and press it to select menu options. <br/><br/>2) Schedule Mode: Use this mode to keep on top of your main lawn and let OcuMow go out according to a set schedule. Set OcuMow 18 to mow as little or as often as you like. For smaller gardens, the mower will need less time to maintain the lawn. <br/><br/>3) Use Drop and Mow (Main Area) if you want to mow the main lawn without changing the schedule. Perfect for one-off mows in between scheduled mowings, or for when you’d rather send the mower out yourself than let it go out automatically. The mower finds its own way back to the charging station. <br/><br/>4) Use Drop and Mow (Other Area) if you want to mow another lawn, for example a front lawn, side lawn or lawn at another property. The mower will wait in standby mode when the battery needs recharging.  <br/></p><p></p>",
            "button_1_style": "",
            "button_1_text": "",
            "button_1_url": "",
